course: dictionary
lesson: 9429
title: Stack: a pile, a lot, or a tall rock
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. «Stack the chairs at the end of the day.» Here stack is a verb: you make a neat pile of chairs, one on top of another.
explain: «I have stacks of homework tonight.» Stacks here does not mean piles of paper. It means a lot of homework. Try your meaning in the sentence: "I have a lot of homework tonight" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «Dropping the stack in the wrong order was a disaster.» Here stack is a noun: the cards were a neat pile, and their order mattered. In the Twelve Apostles sentence, stacks are tall rocks left standing in the sea after the arches fall.
fact: A stack is a neat pile of things, one on top of another.
fact: To stack is to make such a pile, as in «stack the dishwasher».
fact: «Stacks of» is an informal way of saying a lot of: «stacks of homework» means a lot of homework.
fact: A stack can also be a tall chimney.
fact: Check the other words in the sentence: they are the clues that tell you which meaning of stack is meant.
exercise: «Stack the chairs at the end of the day.» What does stack mean here? | To sing loudly | To run away quickly | *To make a neat pile | To count to ten
exercise: «I have stacks of homework tonight.» What does stacks of mean? | Three pieces of homework | Neat piles of paper only | Very tall chimneys | *A lot of
exercise: Find and copy the one word that means a neat pile in this sentence: «Each hole meant a number, and dropping the stack in the wrong order was a disaster.» | number | disaster | *stack | hole
test: «A stack of pancakes is served warm.» What is a stack of pancakes? | A pancake that has been burnt | *A neat pile, one on top of another | A pancake race | A tall chimney
test: «The bones of the spine are stacked in a gentle S-curve.» What does stacked mean here? | Painted red | *Put in a neat pile, one on top of another | Run quickly | Broken into small bits
exam: «Australia's Twelve Apostles are limestone stacks that are slowly collapsing.» Which meaning of stack fits? | A lot of something | A neat pile of things | To make a neat pile | *A tall, pillar-like rock left standing in the sea
